#                   previewer on every cursor move — ~300ms a keystroke, most of
#                   it uv startup and re-parsing fonts that had not changed.
#                   Browsing Google's monospace families is INSIDE it, as the
#                   last row under an opened lane rather than a subcommand. It
#                   prefetches the rows AROUND the cursor, so the one you are
#                   about to reach has already arrived; a shell function
#                   re-execing curl per preview could not do that.
#   font show       what is set, and whether wezterm is honoring it. The picker
#                   rasterizes its own previews, so it looks right whether or
#                   not the lanes are live; `show` prints real SGR 6 and SGR 5
#                   text instead, which is a picture of what wezterm DID.
#
# A bash function would SHADOW that binary — functions win over PATH — which is
# why nothing here is called `font`, and why CI checks for it.


